# DFlash Console — restart after changes

When you finish a task that changed any of these, **automatically restart the Console server** before ending your turn:

- `api/**` or `core/**` (Python backend)
- `config.json`
- `requirements.txt`

## How to restart

From the repo root:

```powershell
.\scripts\restart-console-server.ps1
```

Use `.\run.ps1` only for a full cold start (first run, dependency install, or llama-server port cleanup).

## Static-only changes

Changes under `static/**` or `static/css/**` do **not** require a server restart. Tell the user to hard-refresh the browser (Ctrl+Shift+R) if they do not see UI updates.

## After restart

Confirm the API is up (HTTP 200 from `http://127.0.0.1:8900/` or the configured `ui_port`). Do not ask the user to restart manually when you can run the script yourself.

The open browser tab auto-refreshes when the API comes back (`server-reload-watch.js` + `/api/health` `boot_id`). No need to tell the user to hard-refresh after a backend restart.
